@startuml detail_panel_states
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' detail_panel_states — v28.6, the docked panel's guard machine.
'
' The picture to hold: there is NO arrow out of "Dirty" that skips the
' prompt. Switching tasks, piece clicks, the breadcrumb, the X, and Esc
' all funnel through the same Save/Discard/Stay question — no silent
' discard path exists, which is the explicit-save contract in one glance.
' The modal dialog's path (runTaskDetail's fallback) is the OLD sequence
' diagram, piece_detail_sequence.*, unchanged.
'
' Referenced from design-addendum-detail-panel.md §B.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!include _style.puml

[*] --> Closed
Closed --> Clean : openTask(id)\n(slide in, fresh form, markClean)

Clean --> Dirty : any edit\n(Save button lights)
Dirty --> Clean : Save clicked\n(apply, reseed, "Saved ✓")

Clean --> Clean : navigate / switch task\n(swap in place, no question)
Clean --> Closed : ✕, Esc, or\nclick outside (scrim)

Dirty --> Prompt : navigate, switch,\n✕, Esc, or click outside
Prompt --> Clean : Save\n(apply, then proceed)
Prompt --> Clean : Discard\n(proceed, nothing written)
Prompt --> Dirty : Stay\n(the click did nothing)

note right of Prompt
  Save / Discard / Stay.
  Save is the DEFAULT button:
  Enter never destroys work.
end note

note right of Clean
  changed() while clean:
  reseed to the new truth.
  While dirty: the user's
  edits win; Save writes last.
end note

@enduml
